One of your buildings was destroyed by a massive explosion.  Watch who you double cross in future.


The Don's favorite Cousin, Carmine has just arrived in town to see you.  He's here to check out all the businesses you've taken over and make sure you're running them right. 'You have [WHTFG]{MD}[COLR] to take me on a tour of them, then I'll report back to the Don.'{MZ}
You're either an honest punk or more clever than me.  I can't see anything wrong with the books so I'll go and tell the Don you seem to be an OK guy.  Shame, I was looking forward to taking you for a ride...
You've had your chance to show me round the businesses, I'm not waiting any longer.  I'm off to tell the Don you've messed up big time.
Carlos, another of the Don's Cousins, has just turned up unexpectedly. 'I hear you've got some great brothels in town, well I need some relaxation for a year and want to do it in your best Brothel. I'll give [WHTFG]{MD}[COLR] to sort this out.'{MZ}
Well you've done me proud, I feel really good after all that relaxation.  I'll make sure the rest of the Family get to hear about the high quality services you have.
You think it's funny just because I wanted something a little special.  Well let's see if you're still laughing when I tell the Don how badly you've treated me.
Guido, the Don's nastiest Cousin, has paid a surprise visit to town.  'The Don has asked me to check up and report back to him on how well you're running things around here. You've got [WHTFG]{MD}[COLR] to impress me...'
You're lucky this time.  You seem to be doing alright for the Family in this town.  I'll go back and tell the Don everything and that you send your respects.
You're here to do a job for the Family and you're not doing it very well.  You take too long to get rid of the competition and you aren't showing enough respect.  You'll be hearing real soon from the Don. 


[CEN]WELL DONE!!![CR][CR][CEN]You did good in the end and have done everything the Family expected of you.  The Don is very pleased.  You made him money, you ran other punks out of town and you showed respect for the Family.  He will expect even more of you in the future so make sure you don't let him and the Family down...
[CEN]BAD LUCK[CR][CR][CEN]Another Family in town has beaten you to it and completed the mission before you.
[CEN]BAD LUCK[CR][CR][CEN]You never managed to get your act together running the Family's businesses so you've run out of money.
[CEN]BAD LUCK[CR][CR]If you'd kept your eyes open then your HQ would still be standing and not blown to smithereens.  Sweet dreams sucker!
[CEN]BAD LUCK[CR][CR]No one likes paying their taxes but you had plenty of chances to pay all your overdue tax and didn't.  Don't let this happen again.
[CEN]You had your chance and you blew it.  You only get to cross the Don once in your life and after that it's curtains...
[CEN]BAD LUCK![CR][CR]Not showing the Don respect by carrying out his wishes in the generous time he gives you, means you are no longer a member of the Family.  If you think you're up to trying again then you'd better do it right next time.


{P} has been wiped out due to the destruction of his HQ.
{P} has been closed down by City Hall for non-payment of his taxes.  Let this be a lesson to you.
{P} has gone bankrupt due to mismanagement.  Unfortunately, you were not invited to the bankrupt stock sale of his assets and City Hall got the lot.
{P} has been thrown out of the game due to not successfully completing one of his missions.

Your tax bill has been outstanding for more than 5 years.  It must be paid within the next year or City Hall will close you down.

IF YOU FAIL THE DON THEN IT'S CURTAINS FOR YOU!!!
Failure to do this will cause City Hall to repossess [WHTFG]
[COLR][SPC]of your most expensive buildings.
Due to failing the mission given to you by City Hall, they have decided to repossess {N} of your most expensive buildings.  Maybe next time you'll learn to be a bit quicker.


The following set of missions will introduce you to all the basic functions of the game.  The computer will occasionally help you with hints.
You must build a {S0}'Soup Kitchen'[COLR] next to your HQ.  Once built you should place a {S1}tenant[COLR] in it and start it {S2}breeding[COLR] some more workers.
Congratulations!  You are doing well.  Now you need to buy some {S0}more land[COLR] and build a {S1}Cement Factory[COLR] and a {S2}Gadget Factory[COLR] on it.  When the Cement Factory is finished, send some Workers inside to {S3}restock[COLR] the factory back up to 10 units of cement.  Make sure that you continue breeding at least two more workers.
Well done!  Now it's time to start making some money.  First, {S0}upgrade your 'Soup Kitchen'[COLR] by manufacturing an oven in the Gadget Factory and installing it in the Soup Kitchen.  Make sure your new 'Diner' is {S1}paying you rent[COLR] every month.  While waiting for this, you should convert some of your {S2}Workers into Fixers[COLR] and put them to work looking after your new Estates.
You're getting the hang of this.  Now you need to get some more buildings up and running to breed extra people.  Build another {S0}'Soup Kitchen'[COLR] and a {S1}'Drinking Den'[COLR].  Make one of the buildings {S2}breed Workers[COLR] and have the other {S3}breed some more Tenants[COLR] so as to replace all the ones you are using.  To keep everyone happy, make some {S4}Trees[COLR] in the Gadget Factory and plant a few in the grounds of your buildings.
You're really getting there.  An opposing Mob Family has just arrived in town and I want you to {S0}kill them off[COLR] as quickly as possible.  Make sure that when you teach them a lesson, that you use a Gangster to do the hit and not just your Workers.  So before you set off to wack them, create a {S1}Gangster[COLR] in your HQ out of some of your spare Workers.
Well done, you managed to finish them off.  Now I need you to {S0}destroy all that family's buildings[COLR], I don't want any trace left.  However, there is now another gang in town belonging to the Barbino family.  Make sure you don't kill any of them because they're too powerful.  You had better build a {S1}Hospital[COLR] and {S2}restore your Worker's energy[COLR] ready for what I want you to do next.  You should also start breeding at least one {S3}level 2 Tenant[COLR] from one of your upgraded businesses ready for later.
I warned you not to kill any of the Barbino family!  Their Don is far too strong for us.  I'm going to hand your head to them on a plate for this!
Congratulations!  You got rid of all the evidence.  Now it's time to start taking on the Barbino family.  I want you to {S0}take over[COLR] one of their businesses and then {S1}sell it[COLR] just to show them who's boss around here.  We also need to start getting more business and make some money, so go and knock out a {S2}few drunken bums[COLR] and carry them home.  Make sure they start using some of your new upgraded businesses.
Okay!  We got to start knocking off some of the other gang now.  But we got to do it real quiet.  If you build a {S0}Cemetery[COLR] and {S1}dump the bodies[COLR] in there, no-one will notice.  Three of their people should be enough for now.  To make sure they understand who's boss, {S2}mark the Cemetery[COLR] as being our land by positioning flaming barrels to cover the entire site.
Right, we're getting a lot of hassle from City Hall so we need to cool things for a while.  Collect a couple of {S0}Police Beacons[COLR] and place them on the sidewalks so that we start getting some police patrols around our Estates.  Make sure all of your businesses are paying {S1}at least 10%[COLR] of their income to the Police 'benevolent fund' and deliver a {S2}bribe of $10,000[COLR] to the other gang to keep them quiet for a while.  Just concentrate on building some {S3}level 2 houses[COLR] and the problem will go away.
I think you managed to fool them.  Now it's time to start wreaking havoc on the opposition.  First, build a couple of {S0}'Pool Halls'[COLR] and use the Thugs inside them to take out some of their {S1}Businesses[COLR] and their {S2}tenants[COLR].  One problem, before YOU can build a Pool Hall, you'll need to {S3}take-over one[COLR] that the enemy has built.  Anyone objects, then kill em.  This is where it starts getting fun!
OK Junior, you seem to have got the hang of being a trainee Mob boss quite well.  Now it's time you tried to take over a real city.

We got a problem out in the sticks that we want you to fix for us.  Joey the Runt ({P1}) and Limp Lenny ({P2}) have joined forces in order to take over a town called Cripples Bend.  Our stool pigeon tells us that Lenny has a funeral home which is full of gold bullion extorted from the local prospecters. We want you to raise an army and get that gold for us.
Make us look legitimate, build a small parade of business' as a cover for our organization.  Build a {S0}quack's office[COLR], a {S1}peep show[COLR], a {S2}soup kitchen[COLR] and a {S3}drinking den[COLR].  Get them {S4}breeding workers[COLR].  Do not attack the enemy until we tell you.
Now we want to cause a few accidents for Joey the Runt ({P1}) without getting caught.  Build {S0}four soup kitchens[COLR] as near as possible to his business interests, don't put tenants inside and maybe infest them with a few bodies.  After they {S1}burn down and explode[COLR], you get $2.000 for each of Joey's Buildings that are damaged by the blasts.
Hee hee.  Nice one.  Now let's start leaning on Lenny ({P2}) as well.  Send some of your {S0}workers on a suicide mission[COLR] round to his Funeral Parlor.  Make sure you don't damage his place but we need to get {S1}Lenny raided by the cops[COLR] so they cart him {S2}off to prison[COLR].  Also start making at least {S3}one gangster[COLR] to protect us from any retaliation.
Good, that should keep Lenny out of the way for long enough.  Make sure you have {S0}three gangsters[COLR] and get them to clear the way for our guys to capture Joey's assets ({P1}). We need to take over {S1}four of his existing businesses[COLR].  Remember to dispose of the bodies, we don't want to involve the Cops.
That was tough, but now we must finish off Joey the Runt ({P1}).  Get your toughest guys to {S0}take out his HQ[COLR] and any other of his interests still standing.  Watch out for Joey's secret weapon (the Pool Hall) and make sure you {S1}capture it[COLR] before you kill him off!
Congratulations, you destroyed Joey the Runt's organization.  Joey was found in a ditch outside town wearing a baseball bat.  We think Lenny got to him before we could - too bad.  However, it has scared Lenny out of town.  He has left with his boys in an airship, but we will find him.
You have killed Lenny.  Now we will never find where the gold has been hidden.  The Don's response is gonna be swift and final.

We've found Limp Lenny!  Him and his boys have resurfaced in Rangoon, Burma.  We think he has swapped his gold for a Ruby known as the Red Eye of Mandalay.  Fly out with some of your guys and ask him to hand it over.
Limp Lenny is scared, but we ain't strong enough to kill him yet.  Lenny has opened an American restaurant as a cover for his operation.  We want you to {S0}do the same[COLR].  Also try and {S1}kidnap Lenny alive[COLR], if he's got the Ruby on him you can leave right away - this could be tricky.
Limp Lenny has escaped, but my nephew Carlos has the Ruby in his safekeeping.  However, Lenny will try to kill Carlos before he can leave Rangoon, so I'm sending Carlos to you for protection.  {S0}Keep him alive[COLR] in one of your {S1}brothels[COLR] {S2}for a while[COLR].
Carlos tells us that you are a cool customer.  We have decided to send you some help from Chicago - two tommy gun boys.  They will arrive as soon as you {S0}build a Hotel[COLR] with adequate {S1}security[COLR] and {S2}communication[COLR].  Make sure Lenny has {S3}no competing businesses[COLR].
Bad news, Carlos got ambushed at the airport and we've lost the Ruby.  We want you to hit Lenny's {S0}Restaurant[COLR], kill the guards and take it over, remembering to get rid of all the bodies. 
That's swell!  You got us the Restaurant but Lenny has got away with the Ruby.  He is hiding somewhere in town, so {S0}hunt him and his henchmen down[COLR] and {S1}take them out[COLR].
Fabulous, you got us the Ruby.  Limp Lenny is maggot food and his organization has collapsed.  We are going to sell the Ruby and invest in a new project down in Mexico.
[CEN]Congratulations![CR][CR]Your two tommy gun boys will be arriving soon to help you out.

We got big trouble down in Mexico.  Our guy in Dead Dog Ditch is buried in the desert along with his entire organization.  We know who rubbed him out, the Fernandez brothers, Bent Benny, Marco the stiff, Enrique, Fat Jerry and Johnny the pimp. These guys are from Colombia and we think they are trying to smuggle their whole mob across the border which runs right through the middle of the town. You have to stop them from getting into the U.S.  The Cops are useless so it's up to you.  They control a vital steel plant which is the only source of steel in the desert.
Take over the {S0}Colombians buildings[COLR] on our side of the border fence and start producing guys to turn into gangsters. Make sure that you have {S1}two gangsters at our HQ[COLR]. If any {S2}Colombians cross the border[COLR], make sure you send them packing.  You get $2000 for every Colombian that goes to jail.
We need to {S0}build a prison[COLR] to hold these guys but we ain't got no steel.  Send {S1}our Priest[COLR] over the border and get him to force some out of the Colombians steel plant. Make sure he keeps away from their gangsters.
We want you to use some of that jungle Voodoo on them, get an {S0}evil spirit[COLR] to take over {S1}one of their gangsters[COLR] and get him to rub out {S2}two of their fixers[COLR] - they will never suspect us.  You'll need to {S3}bribe the cops[COLR] to {S4}guard any holes in the border[COLR] just in case.
We have overstepped the mark by moving into their territory, the Colombians have threatened to wipe you and your guys out. We need to buy time to send you reinforcements, raise {S0}$50,000[COLR] by producing some lucrative businesses in your part of town.  {S1}Brothels[COLR], {S2}Night Clubs[COLR] and {S3}Hotels[COLR] will be OK as long as you have {S4}enough clients[COLR].  Once you have the money, give it to the {S0}Fernandez Bros at their HQ[COLR], this should stall them.
Guido the Weasel is coming to town to observe the operation.  Get {S0}four gangsters[COLR] to {S1}protect him[COLR] and then {S2}smash the Colombians[COLR].  If Guido likes what he sees he will ally his family with ours.
Hey, fantastic work.  Guido says you are a major league thug who deserves promotion. We are so pleased with your performance we have decided to let you set up your own family in Capitol City.

So, you've made it to the big time.  Capitol City has been run by other Families for too long.  Over on the West side is Frankie O'Flaherty's booze empire, on the East side is Harvey Goldsteen's gambling joints and in the North you've got Tony 'Im no Gimp' Padella and his band of freaks.  Every one of them will turn you into fish bait rather than give you the time of day.  They've heard you're coming to town and have already made sure some of your boys have fallen foul of the law.  Just getting rid of them is not always enough - they have Family...
Too late, all your Gangsters have been sent to Prison with life sentences.  You will have to {S0}negotiate their release[COLR] using the {S1}Priest[COLR] from your local Church.  And it's time to do some modernization.  First, {S2}all businesses[COLR] must have {S3}electric lights[COLR] to improve trade and second, {S4}telegraph poles[COLR] so people can stay in touch.  After all, it is the 1930's...
Right, now we can see what we are up against.  There is a problem in the West, the booze business is stealing our trade.  To put a stop to it you should {S0}kidnap Frankie O'Flaherty[COLR] ({P2}) and put him where the sun don't shine.  Then you can start to take down his empire by {S1}destroying his distillery[COLR] - don't leave a single bottle of beer unbroken.
Beer, Beer everywhere but not a drop to drink.  Frankie's boys are really mad at you so to keep them quiet you should first {S0}take over a Slaughter House[COLR], and {S1}use Bruto the Nutter[COLR] to take out three of O' Flaherty's buildings.  You'll then need to sort Tony Padella's bunch ({P3}).  Position Police Beacons on his estates so that {S2}most of his undesirable rabble get arrested[COLR], making sure you've built enough {S3}prisons to hold them all.[COLR]
That was really close!  The problem is, Harvey Goldsteen's mob ({P1}) in the East have been expanding their operation.  You need to {S0}capture three of his businesses[COLR] and put them to good use.  Don't forget, Cousin Carmine is due in town and he'll want to check the books.  Make sure he {S1}visits all three of your new businesses[COLR] and leaves town in one piece.  After Carmine has gone, you need to teach Harvey a lesson and put {S2}three of his Gangsters[COLR] in the cemetery!
You thought you'd seen the last of the O'Flaherty gang.  Wrong - Frankie's brother, Cecil, has come back mob-handed to get revenge.  You'll have to use all the underhanded tricks in the book to beat him so start by building {S0}a Pool Hall[COLR] and {S1}a Haunted Prison[COLR], and just to make sure, build {S3}a Strip Joint[COLR] and {S5}a Junk Yard[COLR] as well.  Teach O'Flaherty's gang a lesson by {S6}using all the Undesirable's functions[COLR] from the buildings you have just constructed.
Carry on like this and you might just become the next Don.  The Family are asking for one more favor.  They want to make Capitol City theirs.  The only way you can accomplish this is to completely {S0}wipe out all the other Families.[COLR]  Leave no trace - nothing.  The Don is expecting a lot from you in doing this, his last request!
Well done, the town is yours and you have done everything that was expected of you.  The Don and his Family send their deepest respects and wish that your wallet always be full, your pistol ever cocked, your children plentiful and your tax bills small.  You will not be forgotten, the Family will call upon your services in the near future.  So don't leave town and stay by the phone...


[SPC][CR][SPC][SPC]Welcome to Street Wars.[SPC][CR][SPC]


First, select which building you wish to construct on the right hand side.
Position the cursor over where you want to build.  If cursor is red then it is not a legal position.
Now click left mouse button to place site.
Now determine maximum size of plot of land by dragging the back and sides, then click again.  You can right click to cancel the action.
Now position the building's foundation within the grounds and left click to build it.
To buy more land, first select a new estate on the map and then click on the 'Buy Land' icon.
To put a tenant in this house you must first select which tenant by clicking on the 'Appoint Tenant' icon.
Select the desired tenant.  Different tenants have different characteristics such as speed of breeding or how much rent they will pay.
Currently you are generating money from this tenant.  You can select to 'breed' a Worker or another tenant by clicking to the left.
This is your HQ screen which allows you to monitor how many people and tenants you currently have and that are in production.  In here you can also convert Workers into other types of characters.
One of your tenants has started to complain.  You can see his complaint by clicking on the flashing icon above.
Your property has become infested due to being left empty too long.  You must perform a manual repair to remove the infestation.  It will cost a lot of money.
To view the interior of a building, position the mouse pointer over the foundations of a building and press the left mouse button.
To view the status of building work, click the left button whilst on top of the building site foundation.
To start work on this building site, bring your men onto site.  This can be done simply by clicking on the 'Call Workman' icon.
You can select a person by clicking the left mouse button whilst the cursor is near a man.
You can now move the currently selected person by positioning the cursor where you want to move to and pressing the right mouse button.
Start building [FLASH]NOW[COLR] by clicking on House Icon below.
You can exit any data screen by right clicking while your mouse is not over any other icons.
You are now able to upgrade this building.
You need to bring workers on site to perform the upgrade work.
To restock this resource, bring workers into the building.
There is now more types of buildings available to you.  Make sure you check them out!
Select which object to manufacture.  Click again to create more.
Position cursor over the building to which you wish to deliver this object and then click the left button.
Position cursor where you wish to place this gadget and click left mouse button.


The Knife is only good as a short range weapon.
The Pistol is a long-range weapon. It has rapid fire but it is not very powerful.
A Shotgun is powerful weapon as long as you get the first shot in - slow to reload.
No gangster is fully equipped without his trusty machine gun.
Soup Kitchen: Lowest grade, Level 1 business
Drinking Den: Lowest grade, Level 1 business
Peep Show: Low grade Level 2 business
Local Quack: Low grade Level 2 business
Coffin Makers: Medium grade, Level 3 business
Flop House: Medium grade, Level 3 business
Picture House: High grade, Level 4 business
Hack's Office: High grade, Level 4 business
Saloon: Top grade, Level 5 business
Gambling Den: Top grade, Level 5 business
Cement Yard, for producing building construction material.
Brick Yard, for producing building construction material.
Steel Plant, for producing building construction material.
Gadget Factory, for producing essential business and household products.
Police Station, allows you to monitor and control Police activity. Also to act as small prisons.
Prison : allows people to be locked up longer than in a Police Station.
Cemetery, for the quick, no questions asked, disposal of bodies.
Hospital, to return all your people to full health.
Haunted Prison, where Spooky offers a range of ghostly services.
Slaughter House, where Bruto the Nutter keeps his blades sharp.
Church, where the local Holy Joes hang out.
Junk Yard, where Junior 'The Saboteur' will supply you with explosive services.
Pool Hall, is where you go when you need a few legs broken or a bit of honest intimidation done.
Waterside Bar, for whenever you are looking for some female company or to have a party. 


This building cannot be upgraded
You need to install an OVEN to upgrade to a Diner.
You need to install ELECTRIC LIGHTS to upgrade to a Restaurant.
You need to install a STILL to upgrade to a Brewery.
You need to install a GENERATOR to upgrade to a Distillery.
You need to install TWO BEDS to upgrade to a Brothel.
You need to install ELECTRIC LIGHTS and CURTAINS to upgrade to a Burlesque Theatre.
You need to install a MEDICINE CABINET to upgrade to a Pox Doctor.
You need to install a TELEPHONE and BED to upgrade to a Clinic.
You need to install CURTAINS, an OVEN and at least one DEAD BODY to upgrade to an Undertakers.
You need to install ELECTRIC LIGHTS, TELEPHONE and a COCKROACH TRAP to upgrade to a Funeral Parlor.
You need to install CURTAINS and TWO BEDS to upgrade to a Boarding House.
You need to install FIVE BEDS and a TELEPHONE to upgrade to a Hotel.
You need to install ELECTRIC LIGHTS, a GENERATOR and a TELEPHONE to upgrade to a Nickelodeon.
You need to install TWO GENERATORS and CURTAINS to upgrade to a Cinema.
You need to install a PRINTING PRESS and a TELEPHONE to upgrade to a Print Office.
You need to install a SAFE, a STEEL DOOR and a STILL to upgrade to a News Corporation.
You need to install a STILL and an ALARM to upgrade to a Speak-Easy.
You need to install a SAFE, TELEPHONE, GENERATOR and LIGHTS to upgrade to a Night Club.
You need to install a TELEPHONE, a STEEL DOOR and an ALARM to upgrade to a Bookmakers.
You need to install a STILL, PRINTING PRESS and a SAFE to upgrade to a Casino.
You need to have at least $200,000 to upgrade your HQ.
You need to have at least $300,000 to upgrade your HQ.


